    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "When you were sleeping only a few hours a night and feeling that energy and productivity, were you also experiencing periods of feeling unusually happy, excited, or elevated in your mood—or was it more just about having the energy and motivation to work?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Um... well, I want to be completely honest with you, even though I'm a little embarrassed to admit this next part. I really don't want you to think I'm a bad person. \n\nBut yes, I did feel really happy during those times. Actually, I'd be flying high, just feeling so incredibly good, like I could fix every single car in town all by myself. It felt like a positive thing at first, you know? Being that motivated and confident. \n\nBut... gosh, I feel terrible saying this because I really try to be kind to everyone... my mood would sometimes just snap. Like, if I was in that zone and my husband just asked a simple question about why the dishes weren't done, or if one of the other techs at the shop just moved my socket set... I would just blow up. I'd get so angry, like they were purposely trying to hold me down or ruin my momentum. \n\nI always feel so guilty about it afterward, because I really am not a mean person, I promise. I don't want you to think I'm a bad wife or a difficult coworker. I just get so wrapped up in doing a good job. Is it... I mean, is it okay that I get a little snappy like that when I'm just trying to work hard? I hope you can understand where I'm coming from.",
